WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.266
Have you

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.433
seen these images

00:00:01.433 --> 00:00:03.333
coming out of Azerbaijan?

00:00:03.333 --> 00:00:04.133
A hundred thousand

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:05.633
people have fled their homes.

00:00:05.633 --> 00:00:06.633
Let me show you on the map

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:07.500
why this has happened.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.433
We're talking about a region up here.

00:00:09.433 --> 00:00:10.766
It's called the Caucasus,

00:00:10.766 --> 00:00:11.900
these two countries,

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.233
Azerbaijan and Armenia.

00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:14.133
There's been a lot of tension

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.633
between these two about borders,

00:00:15.633 --> 00:00:17.433
which is why you have all these enclaves.

00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:19.200
One of these borders is right here.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.966
The region of Nagorno-Karabakh.

00:00:20.966 --> 00:00:22.000
Ethnic Armenians

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.400
have lived here for decades

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.333
and have been trying

00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.633
to make their own state

00:00:25.633 --> 00:00:27.033
within Azerbaijan.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.133
Azerbaijan has tried

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:29.766
to drive them out for decades.

00:00:29.766 --> 00:00:32.066
But Russia, who's just right up here,

00:00:32.066 --> 00:00:33.133
has been the one kind

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.066
of keeping the peace,

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.833
keeping stability between the two.

00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:37.466
But Russia has turned its attention

00:00:37.466 --> 00:00:38.866
towards its war in Ukraine.

00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:39.633
So Azerbaijan,

00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:40.833
with the support of their neighbor

00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:42.133
Turkey, has kicked out

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.433
almost everyone in this enclave

00:00:44.433 --> 00:00:46.433
and pushed them into Armenia.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:47.700
And that's what we're looking at

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.566
in this imagery.

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:50.000
All of this is a sign of Russia's

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.900
waning influence in the Caucasus

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.500
and an increase of Turkey's

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.300
influence there.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.333
If you want to better understand

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:57.533
international politics, follow for more.

